            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThe `@call.inner` Lua query [uses `#match!` directive](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/5ca4aaa6efdcc59be46b95a3e876300cfead05ef/queries/lua/textobjects.scm#L10) that is not recognized by Neovim itself (and hence [by `MiniAi.gen_spec.treesitter()`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/429e5f9dc9cd59bf76cd98b687300f0a384a7f52/doc/mini-ai.txt#L770-L774)).\n\nThe suggestions are:\n- Use `main` branch of both 'nvim-treesitter' and 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' (recommended). Here is an [example from MiniMax](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/c419b993bee83a3494d55ae7063b0cdbad5c5af5/configs/nvim-0.11/plugin/40_plugins.lua#L32-L71).\n- Set [`opts.use_nvim_treesitter`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/429e5f9dc9cd59bf76cd98b687300f0a384a7f52/doc/mini-ai.txt#L786) when creating a textobjects (not recommended long term).",
